course: dictionary
lesson: 7897
title: Raptor: a bird or a dinosaur?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word raptor has two. Its main meaning is a bird of prey: a bird that hunts other animals with strong feet, sharp curved claws called talons, and a hooked beak. Eagles, hawks, falcons and owls are all raptors.
explain: The second meaning is informal. People use raptor as a short name for some meat-eating dinosaurs, especially Velociraptor. To choose the right meaning, read the clues. «In the films, raptors are as tall as a man» is about dinosaurs, but «like hawks today» is about birds. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about real birds or about dinosaurs?
fact: A raptor is a bird of prey. It hunts other animals.
fact: Raptors have strong feet, sharp curved claws called talons, and a hooked beak.
fact: A raptor's foot has three main toes forward and a small toe at the back, built from the same bones as a chicken's foot.
fact: In dinosaur talk, raptors are meat-eating dinosaurs, but «the real Velociraptor was about the size of a turkey and covered in feathers.»
fact: «Utahraptor was about 6 metres long» and lived earlier than Velociraptor. Most raptors were small.
exercise: «In the films, raptors are as tall as a man, scaly, and clever enough to open doors» Here, raptors are | Fish in a river | Birds at a bird table | *Dinosaurs | Trees in a forest
exercise: «Raptors held their big curved toe claw off the ground while walking.» Find and copy the word that names the sharp, curved part. | scientist | trackway | pack | *claw
exercise: Which sentence is about real birds of prey today? | *«Raptors held their big curved toe claw off the ground while walking and probably used it to pin down prey, like hawks today.» | «Utahraptor was about 6 metres long and as heavy as a polar bear.» | «In the films, raptors are as tall as a man, scaly, and clever enough to open doors.» | «A few trackways show raptors walking together.»
test: Raptor has an informal meaning. What does it mean in this sentence? «Utahraptor lived earlier than Velociraptor.» | *A meat-eating dinosaur | A small, sweet fruit | A hidden cave | A bird that sings at dawn
test: Which animal is a raptor, a bird of prey? | Rabbit | Goldfish | Dolphin | *Falcon
exam: Read «Utahraptor was about 6 metres long and as heavy as a polar bear, and lived earlier than Velociraptor; most raptors were small.» Which meaning of raptor fits best? | A small, sweet fruit | A bird that sings beautifully | *A meat-eating dinosaur | A type of ship
